## Pictures in your text

To add a picture, place the cursor where it goes and choose *Document ▸ Insert image…*. You
can also drop a picture file on the text, or paste one.

A picture is never drawn wider than the text around it. A wide screenshot is shown at the
width of the text, its height in proportion. Its own size is kept: widen the window or the
text column and it grows back, up to that size.

## Changing a picture

Click a picture to select it. Its menu, from a right click or the *Image* menu, offers:

- *View the image*, to look at it full size;
- *Open in another app*, to open it in the application your system uses for pictures;
- *Describe the image…*, for a reader who cannot see it;
- *Resize the image…*, as a percentage of the size it is shown at: 50 halves it;
- *Original size*, to go back to the picture's own size.

You can also drag a corner of a selected picture to resize it.

## The image viewer

Double-click a picture, or choose *View the image*, to open the viewer. It shows the picture
as large as the window allows.

- *Zoom in*, *Zoom out*, *Fit* and *100 %* change its size. So do the + and − keys, 0 for
  *Fit* and 1 for *100 %*.
- Hold Ctrl and turn the mouse wheel to zoom where you point. On a trackpad, pinch.
- Drag the picture to move around it when it is larger than the window.
- The left and right arrow keys go to the previous and next picture.
- *Save a copy…* writes the picture to a file of your choice.

Press Escape, or *Close* at the right end of the bar, to close the viewer.

A Book's cover opens there too: on the Book's page, choose *View* beside the cover, or
double-click it.

## The gallery of a notes folder

A notes folder has a *Gallery* view, beside *Notes*, *Story bible* and *Overview*. It shows the
pictures in the folder's notes as thumbnails. Each thumbnail keeps its picture's proportions.

Choose what it shows:

- *First image* gives one thumbnail per note, with the number of its other pictures. *All
  images* gives one per picture.
- *Nested* shows each subfolder as a tile with its first four pictures. Double-click it to go
  inside; the path at the top takes you back. *Flat* shows every picture of the folder and its
  subfolders at once.
- *Notes without images* adds the notes that hold only text, as tiles of their opening words.
- *Image size* makes the thumbnails smaller or larger.

These choices apply to every gallery you open.

## Finding a picture

The gallery shares its search field, its tag and status filters and its order with the
*Overview*. What you narrow in one view is narrowed in the other.

Double-click a thumbnail, or press Enter, to open it in the image viewer. The arrow keys then
go through the pictures the gallery shows, in its order. Right-click a thumbnail and choose
*Open the note* to open the note it is in.

## Research from Scrivener

A Scrivener project's research pictures arrive as resources of the folder they sat in (see
[Coming from Scrivener](:help-import-scrivener) and [Files and links for your
research](:help-resources)). Open that folder and choose *Gallery* to see them with the other
pictures, marked *Resource*.
